    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$2 \\mathrm{eV}$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$5 \\mathrm{eV}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "For an insulator, $E_{\\mathrm{g}}>3 \\mathrm{eV}$, that is why electron transition from valence band to conduction band is not possible. For semiconductor $E_{\\mathrm{g}}$ is $0.2 \\mathrm{eV}$ to $0.3 \\mathrm{eV}$, while for metals $E_g>5 \\mathrm{eV}$."
  }
